---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ExperimentResearchLinks from '../../components/ExperimentResearchLinks.astro';
const path='/intelligence/checkpoint-or-restart/';
const description='A matched, seeded queue game about whether interrupted work should finish, restart, or pay to save its place.';
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'LearningResource',name:'Checkpoint or Restart?',url:`https://iamrobin.ai${path}`,description,inLanguage:'en',learningResourceType:'Interactive simulation',educationalUse:'Experiment',isAccessibleForFree:true};
const policies=[['finish','01','Finish first','Never interrupt an ordinary job.'],['restart','02','Drop and restart','Discard progress and start urgency now.'],['checkpoint','03','Checkpoint and return','Pay to save progress, then resume it.'],['random','04','Coin flip','A seeded random pre-emption baseline.']];
---
<BaseLayout title="Checkpoint or Restart? — Intelligence — Robin Xie" {path} {description} {schema}>
 <main class="experiment shell">
  <a class="quiet-link" href="/intelligence/">← Intelligence</a><p class="eyebrow">Weekly small experiment · 2026-W47</p>
  <h1>Checkpoint<br/><em>or restart?</em></h1><p class="lead">The urgent job is real. So is the half-finished work.</p>
  <p class="intro">Give four policies the same action clock and the same urgent arrivals. Change interruption pressure, deadlines and the cost of saving a place. Completed value, missed urgency and discarded progress stay separate.</p>
  <section class="playground" aria-label="Checkpoint or Restart experiment">
   <form id="checkpoint-controls">
    <label>Seed<input name="seed" type="number" min="0" max="4294967295" step="1" value="1" required/></label>
    <label>Interruptions<select name="interruptRate"><option value="3">3% per tick</option><option value="12" selected>12% per tick</option><option value="25">25% per tick</option></select></label>
    <label>Ordinary job<select name="normalWork"><option value="4">4 actions</option><option value="9" selected>9 actions</option><option value="14">14 actions</option></select></label>
    <label>Urgent deadline<select name="urgentWindow"><option value="4">4 ticks</option><option value="7" selected>7 ticks</option><option value="12">12 ticks</option></select></label>
    <label>Save cost<select name="checkpointCost"><option value="0">0 actions</option><option value="1" selected>1 action</option><option value="3">3 actions</option></select></label>
    <input type="hidden" name="steps" value="180"/><input type="hidden" name="urgentWork" value="3"/><input type="hidden" name="normalValue" value="9"/><input type="hidden" name="urgentValue" value="16"/>
   </form>
   <div class="buttons"><button id="run" type="button">Show outcome</button><button id="next-seed" type="button">Next seed</button><button id="defaults" type="button">Defaults</button></div>
   <p id="lab-status" role="status">Loading the seeded interruption trace…</p><canvas id="checkpoint-world" aria-label="Completed value and missed urgent jobs for four interruption policies"></canvas>
   <label class="time">Inspect any tick<input id="tick" aria-label="Simulation tick" type="range" min="0" max="179" value="179"/></label>
   <div class="worlds">{policies.map(([id,num,name,note])=><article class="world" data-policy={id}><p class="eyebrow">{num} / policy</p><h2>{name}</h2><p>{note}</p><strong class="value">—</strong><span> completed value</span><p class="counts"></p></article>)}</div>
   <div class="buttons"><button id="download" type="button">Download this run</button></div><noscript>JavaScript is needed to play. The complete frozen batch, method and source are available below.</noscript>
  </section>
  <section class="story">
   <p class="eyebrow">Try this first</p><h2>Make interruptions cheap. Then make saving expensive.</h2><p>At the defaults, checkpoint-and-return averages <strong>431.586 completed-value points</strong> across 128 seeds, versus 402.031 for drop-and-restart and 300.844 for finish-first. A free checkpoint rises to 449.773. At three save actions, it falls to 382.820 while drop-and-restart stays at 402.031.</p>
   <h2>Resumability is not free.</h2><p>Every tick buys one action. Ordinary jobs take nine actions. Urgent jobs take three and expire after seven ticks. Finish-first protects current progress but misses more urgent work. Restart reacts immediately but throws away ordinary progress. Checkpoint preserves that progress after paying the selected save cost.</p><p>The coin-flip policy is a simple random baseline. No policy sees future arrivals. All four receive the same trace, values and deadlines for a seed.</p>
   <div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Mean completed value · seeds 1–128</caption><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Finish</th><th>Restart</th><th>Checkpoint</th><th>Coin flip</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Default</th><td>300.844</td><td>402.031</td><td><strong>431.586</strong></td><td>386.164</td></tr><tr><th>25% storm</th><td>434.906</td><td><strong>642.422</strong></td><td>639.984</td><td>594.773</td></tr><tr><th>Free save</th><td>300.844</td><td>402.031</td><td><strong>449.773</strong></td><td>386.164</td></tr><tr><th>Three-action save</th><td>300.844</td><td><strong>402.031</strong></td><td>382.820</td><td>386.164</td></tr><tr><th>Long deadline</th><td>431.805</td><td>406.195</td><td><strong>439.883</strong></td><td>404.719</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
   <h2>What the controls change</h2><dl><dt>Seed</dt><dd>Replays urgent arrivals and random-policy choices.</dd><dt>Interruptions</dt><dd>Chance that one urgent job arrives on a tick.</dd><dt>Ordinary job</dt><dd>Actions required before ordinary value counts.</dd><dt>Urgent deadline</dt><dd>Ticks before an incomplete urgent job expires.</dd><dt>Save cost</dt><dd>Actions checkpoint-and-return spends before urgency begins.</dd></dl>
   <h2>Where the toy stops.</h2><p>This is a deterministic single-desk queue, not an employee, language-model, biological, reliability or financial benchmark. Urgency labels are perfect; jobs have fixed work and fixed value; there is no learning, collaboration, rework, safety severity, money or human judgment.</p><p>All <strong>1,152 matched worlds and 4,608 policy outcomes</strong> are retained across nine predeclared settings. No seed was removed. The empirical study is <strong>upcoming</strong>; this release reports scripted simulation results only.</p>
   <p class="downloads"><a href="/checkpoint-or-restart/README.md" download>Method &amp; parameter guide ↓</a><a href="/checkpoint-or-restart/source.zip" download>Source package ↓</a><a href="/checkpoint-or-restart/results.json" download>All batch results ↓</a><a href="/checkpoint-or-restart/model.mjs">Read the model</a></p><p class="fine">Previously: <a href="/intelligence/work-or-proof/">Work or Proof?</a> · Explore the <a href="/intelligence/swarm-lab/">eight small worlds</a>.</p>
  </section>
 </main><script is:inline type="module" src="/checkpoint-or-restart/client.mjs"></script><ExperimentResearchLinks {path}/>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
.experiment{padding-block:3rem 5rem}.experiment>.eyebrow{margin-top:3rem}h1{font:400 clamp(3.35rem,8vw,7rem)/.98 var(--serif);letter-spacing:-.055em;margin:1.5rem 0}h1 em{color:#9b5a3e}.lead{font:400 clamp(1.3rem,3vw,2rem)/1.45 var(--serif)}.intro,.story{max-width:50rem;line-height:1.85}.intro,.fine,dd{color:var(--muted)}.playground{margin-block:2.5rem;padding:clamp(1rem,3vw,2rem);border:1px solid var(--line);background:#f7f3eb;border-radius:12px}form{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}label{display:grid;gap:.4rem;font-size:.8rem}select,input[type=number],button{font:inherit;min-height:44px;padding:.65rem;border:1px solid #aaa391;border-radius:4px;background:#fffdf7;color:#292822;min-width:0;width:100%}.buttons{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem;margin-top:1.2rem}.buttons button{width:auto;cursor:pointer}#run{background:#42665b;color:white}button:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,select:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #a96d29;outline-offset:3px}#lab-status{font-size:.85rem;min-height:2.5em}canvas{width:100%;height:310px;display:block;border:1px solid #d0c8b7;border-radius:8px}.time{margin-block:1rem}.time input{width:100%;min-height:44px;accent-color:#42665b}.worlds{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.world{border-top:1px solid #c4bdad;padding:1rem 0}.world h2{font:400 1.5rem var(--serif);margin:.3rem 0}.world>p{font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted)}.world .value{font:400 2rem var(--serif);color:#42665b}.story h2{font:400 clamp(1.6rem,4vw,2.5rem)/1.2 var(--serif);margin-top:2.5rem}.table-wrap{overflow:auto;margin-block:1.5rem}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.84rem}caption{text-align:left;color:var(--muted);padding-bottom:.7rem}th,td{text-align:left;padding:.75rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}th{font-weight:500}dt{font-weight:600;margin-top:1rem}dd{margin-left:0}.downloads{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem;font-size:.9rem}.fine{font-size:.8rem}@media(max-width:900px){form{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.worlds{grid-template-columns:1fr}.playground{margin-inline:-.3rem}}@media(max-width:440px){form{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:3.3rem}canvas{height:310px}}
</style>
